 "why": "This is the commonest real decision and no document answers it. The Italian guideline recommends biopsy specifically to identify exon 3 and sonic hedgehog adenomas (its PICO 9) and simultaneously keeps 5 cm as the resection trigger (its PICO 11), without specifying which governs when they disagree. The review of the WHO 6th-edition classification states that exon 3 adenomas are resected whatever their size, but cites no cohort. EASL's rule is explicitly size-first and subtype-blind above the threshold. The molecular data support subtype in both directions — 2 of 14 women with an at-risk profile under 5 cm transformed against 1 of 101 without — but on two events. Write the precedence rule down, with the proviso that it will be applied to a subtype assignment that is often made without sequencing.",
