files.old:
 "why": "The sotorasib pancreatic cohort pooled 38 patients across phase 1 dose exploration, phase 1 expansion and phase 2, with <b>no prespecified response benchmark and no hypothesis test</b>, and its response interval (10% to 37%) is compatible with the under-10% historical benchmark the authors invoke. Adagrasib's prespecified 10% null applies to the pooled tumour-agnostic cohort of 57 evaluable patients, not to its 21 pancreatic patients, and six patients counted as evaluable by investigators were removed by central review for having no measurable disease, moving the denominator favourably. Zenocutuzumab's 36 pancreatic patients were <b>all KRAS wild-type</b>, its primary endpoint was investigator-assessed response with blinded central review only secondary, its primary efficacy population is a post-enrolment construct (204 treated to 158 evaluable, with short-follow-up exclusions falling on early progressors), and no progression-free or overall survival is reported for the pancreatic subgroup at all. None of the three reports a screening denominator, so the testing burden implied by any of them is invisible. The NTRK, RET, BRAF and FGFR entries were not retrieved for this depot."
},
{
 "t": "RASolute 302's hazard ratio of 0.40 is the largest effect on this page, it is established only in RAS G12 disease, and it is inseparable from how badly its comparator arm was delivered.",
 "why": "The dual primary endpoints were met in the RAS G12 population: median overall survival 13.2 versus 6.6 months, hazard ratio 0.40, P<0.001, and progression-free survival by blinded central review 7.3 versus 3.5 months, hazard ratio 0.45. In patients <b>without</b> a G12 mutation the hazard ratio was 1.38 (95% CI 0.60–3.17), a point estimate favouring chemotherapy. And 38 of 252 patients (15.1%) allocated to chemotherapy never received it, against 7 of 248 (2.8%) allocated daraxonrasib — 29 of them withdrawing, and some no longer eligible because ECOG had risen above 1 by the time treatment was due, which an oral agent started the same day does not face. Those patients remain in the comparator's intention-to-treat survival curve. The comparator itself was unconstrained investigator's choice given per local prescribing practice, with a 6.6-month median at the low end of published second-line outcomes, and its quality is not auditable from the report. The sponsor supported the trial and performed and validated the analyses. The direction of the result is not in doubt; the magnitude should be read with the comparator in view."
},
