  "pref": "NANETS states that patients with poorly differentiated carcinoma, small or large cell, should not undergo resection, given the aggressive behaviour and extremely poor prognosis that does not appear to be affected by surgery. ENETS 2023 allows that surgery can benefit localised disease after extensive preoperative imaging, and places carboplatin with etoposide first line in metastatic disease, with irinotecan and a fluoropyrimidine as the best-evidenced second line; median survival in metastatic disease is 11 to 12 months.",
