files.old:
{
 "n": 8,
 "q": "How is growth defined — and is duct growth recorded as well as cyst growth?",
 "why": "There are four definitions, not three: Kyoto 2.5 mm per year, ACG more than 3 mm per year, Fukuoka 2017 5 mm over 2 years, the European guideline 5 mm per year. Kyoto adopted 2.5 because it was the value most frequently reported among candidates spanning 0.96 to 3.5 mm per year, which is a choice by vote frequency rather than performance. None has published measurement reproducibility and 2.5 mm is inside the range over which two readers can disagree. Separately, in the one cohort that measured both, the increase in main pancreatic duct diameter over 5 years predicted later carcinoma (SHR 1.71 per mm, 1.44 to 2.03) and the increase in cyst size did not (1.46, 0.96 to 2.20) — and no guideline records duct growth, Kyoto having considered and rejected it for lack of evidence.",
 "audit": "Report completeness for size and duct diameter; proportion of progression events declared on a same-modality comparison."
