 "q": "Is a local 'suspicious' cytology treated as an absolute surgical indication here, and who reads it?",
 "why": "Kyoto 2024 makes suspicious or positive cytology a high-risk stigma and puts the absolute risk of high-grade dysplasia or invasive carcinoma at 91 to 100% and 100% for those two readings. The same document puts the overall sensitivity of cyst fluid cytology at 28.7% (4.8 to 61.5%), and 59 to 60% of specimens were less than optimal or unsatisfactory for cytology in the two large molecular series. The result is decisive one way and nearly uninformative the other, and it now sits inside the risk classification, so the programme needs a named cytopathology arrangement and an agreed vocabulary before it acts on the word 'suspicious'.",
 "audit": "Cytology category reported per aspirate, specimen adequacy, decision taken, and final histology where an operation followed."
