 "pref": "NCCN defines good performance status as ECOG 0–1 <i>with good biliary drainage and adequate nutritional intake</i>, intermediate as ECOG 2 and poor as ECOG 3 — so drainage and nutrition are part of the eligibility assessment, not a separate matter. For pancreatobiliary and mixed type with good or intermediate status: albumin-bound paclitaxel–gemcitabine, capecitabine–gemcitabine, cisplatin–gemcitabine, cisplatin–durvalumab–gemcitabine, or FOLFOX; with ECOG 0–1 only, also FOLFIRINOX or modified FOLFIRINOX and NALIRIFOX. For poor performance status, palliative and best supportive care are preferred.",
 "avoid": "Do not treat any of these backbones as validated in this disease. ABC-02 randomised 410 patients with locally advanced or metastatic cholangiocarcinoma, gallbladder cancer or ampullary cancer to cisplatin–gemcitabine or gemcitabine, giving median overall survival 11.7 against 8.1 months (hazard ratio 0.64, 95% CI 0.52–0.80, P<0.001) and progression-free survival 8.0 against 5.0 months (P<0.001) — but the number of ampullary patients was not reported, so the ampullary effect size is unknown; that trial is cited here from its abstract and from guideline text only. The FOLFIRINOX and modified FOLFIRINOX options arrive from PRODIGE-24 and the gemcitabine-based ones partly from ESPAC-4, both of which were trials of pancreatic <i>ductal</i> adenocarcinoma that excluded nonductal tumours by protocol, and PRODIGE-24 produced grade 3 or 4 toxicity in 75.9% of a population restricted to performance status 0–1 and age under 80. NCCN states that data for systemic therapy in ampullary cancer are very limited and that the recommendations are extrapolated from pancreatic, colorectal and biliary tract cancer.",
 "note": "Intestinal-type regimens follow the colorectal pattern and pancreatobiliary regimens the pancreatic and biliary pattern — which is a reasonable inference from the genomic concordance, and still an inference built on a morphological call with an interobserver κ of 0.39. Graded D rather than C because not one of the regimens on these lists has been tested in a trial that reports an ampullary population: the nearest, ABC-02, included ampullary patients without counting them, and the rest excluded nonductal tumours outright. Clinical trial entry should be screened at the same visit, and in this setting that is the strongest single recommendation on the assessment. [PROTOCOL]"
},
