 "proposal_locator": "Gate 10 · Standard 'Hepatocellular adenoma is not a standardised MELD exception…' and the gate's ratification note; Decisions this programme still has to make #10 (rationale and audit)",
 "rationale": "Hepatocellular adenoma is not a standardised exception. The whole indication rests on 142 US transplants over 33 years with 18.3% mortality over a median 62.9 months and 9.0% waitlist mortality in patients of median age 34.5 and median MELD 8 — so almost all of that mortality is treatment-attributable — plus 49 European adenomatosis transplants with three operative deaths, five retransplantations, three fatal recurrences and true transformation in only 17 of 49 explants. The US registry records neither the number nor the size of the adenomas; the European one miscoded a quarter of its cases; neither has a comparison group managed without transplantation; and 61.3% of US recipients received exception points while about a tenth met the stated criteria. Graft stewardship for a benign disease is an institutional judgement, and it should be made with those numbers in front of the committee.",
 "audit": "Registry required if opened: route named, lesion dataset, review-board decision, waitlist events, donor source, explant concordance, graft and patient survival."
