 "rationale": "The commonest failure in metastatic PDAC is a genomic report that arrives after the patient is too unwell to act on it, which is an operational problem with a named-owner solution. The sequencing question is separate: RASolute 302 is a phase 3 result with dual primary endpoints met in the RAS G12 population (median overall survival 13.2 versus 6.6 months, HR 0.40; progression-free survival 7.3 versus 3.5 months, HR 0.45), but the benefit is not established outside G12 (non-G12 HR 1.38, 0.60–3.17), 38 of 252 patients (15.1%) allocated to the comparator never received it against 7 of 248 (2.8%) on daraxonrasib, and the comparator was unconstrained investigator's choice with a 6.6-month median at the low end of published second-line outcomes. The local position depends on availability, regulatory status and cost, and should state which RAS alterations it covers. [PAYER]",
